- **P2 — Unaccounted admission scan during append rollback.** [builder.rs:254](/Users/megasoft78/Desktop/Freelance/vexel/rust/crates/vexel-scene/src/builder.rs:254) scans the entire admission registry without work accounting. Failed publication invokes this through [shape_builder.rs:185](/Users/megasoft78/Desktop/Freelance/vexel/rust/crates/vexel-scene/src/shape_builder.rs:185), even though no admissions were created since that append’s checkpoint. Repeated failures can therefore perform uncharged linear work. Avoid this scan for append-local rollback while preserving unconditional cleanup.

- **P2 — “Partial publication” cancellation and panic tests never reach partial edge publication.** [shape_publication.rs:212](/Users/megasoft78/Desktop/Freelance/vexel/rust/crates/vexel-scene/tests/shape_publication.rs:212) and [shape_publication.rs:236](/Users/megasoft78/Desktop/Freelance/vexel/rust/crates/vexel-scene/tests/shape_publication.rs:236) allow only one `Edge` charge, but path validation charges every edge before publication starts. These injections stop during validation—or before the first published edge for a single-edge input. Set the threshold from the input’s edge count so interruption occurs after an actual push, then verify cleanup and surviving-token usability.

- **P2 — Required failure-priority coverage remains incomplete.** [shape_publication.rs:103](/Users/megasoft78/Desktop/Freelance/vexel/rust/crates/vexel-scene/tests/shape_publication.rs:103) tests shape admission alone, without competing malformed stroke/provider failures. The capacity test at [shape_publication.rs:730](/Users/megasoft78/Desktop/Freelance/vexel/rust/crates/vexel-scene/tests/shape_publication.rs:730) exhausts the budget before the first admission-registry allocation, so it never exercises failure while reserving actual shape/serial metadata. Add public-API sequencing assertions and targeted capacity-growth cases to establish the work order’s stated priority contract.

